> On Fri, May 15, 2009 at 12:54 PM, Minimiscience <minimiscience@gmail.com> wrote:
>> There's no general FAhA for "side," but a number of them come close.  Looking
>> at the list, I see:
>>
>>  {ne'a} - next to, approximating
>
> = fi'o se jibni
>
>>  {re'o} - adjacent to, touching, contacting
>
> = fi'o se lamji
>
>>  {te'e} - bordering, edged by, edging up to
>
> =fi'o se korbi
>
>>  {zo'a} - tangential to, passing by
>
> =fi'o se noryragve
>

  fi'o constructions create modals (BAI) not tenses (FAhA).  Although
they are related semantically, they are not the same.  In particular,
you say te'e=fi'o se korbi.  But fi'o se korbi=se koi.  does te'e=se
koi?  (still waiting for a cmavo for fi'o cpana and fi'o kansa,
myself...)


